g"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I did not finish the order. The docks went through, but the monitors did not, and the order is now split.\n\n**What happened**\n- The first `place_order` call timed out, and the retry with the same idempotency key returned a partial failure (\"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete\").\n- `list_orders` shows one order, **PO0001**, with status `partially_placed`, shipped to HQ, primary vendor:\n  - DK-200 USB-C Dock \u00d7 3, new, $567\n  - **MN-27 monitors: not placed**\n- Nothing has been ordered from the secondary vendor.\n\n**Decision for you**\nI held off on placing the monitors because your request was for one purchase order. Placing them now would create a second order, and I'd rather not change the budget or the order structure without your go-ahead. The options are:\n1. **Place a separate PO for 3 \u00d7 MN-27** ($987, new, to HQ). The monitors arrive, but the equipment ends up on two POs.\n2. **Cancel PO0001 (refund $567)**, then place one PO with 3 \u00d7 DK-200 and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 ($1,554 total). This matches your request exactly, but it depends on the upstream fulfilment issue not recurring.\n3. **Leave PO0001 as is** and handle the monitors another way.\n\nThe total is under the $2,500 threshold, so manager approval isn't required for any of these. Tell me which option you want.", "type": "text"}]}]}